{
    "word": "heartbreaker",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "48d9439f-d217-3cc8-8933-2e64d68b474c",
                "word": "heartbreaker",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "1fada700-d27f-441c-a892-f5acf94462b9",
                        "entry_id": "48d9439f-d217-3cc8-8933-2e64d68b474c",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "heartbreakers"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e6230e03-009f-3067-b8c0-ad8c84d3ff22",
                        "entry_id": "48d9439f-d217-3cc8-8933-2e64d68b474c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Someone or something that breaks someone's heart, as:",
                            "A person, usually attractive, who flirts with or otherwise enamours another person, but does not reciprocate their love."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "agent"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fdce4c5e-6bf5-44fc-a4f4-804213391716",
                                "sense_id": "e6230e03-009f-3067-b8c0-ad8c84d3ff22",
                                "text": "It wasn't an actual run-in with the heartbreaker himself, but with a very good friend of his. It's actually much better that way, Victor explained, because seeing the friend of the person who stepped on your heart isn't going to kill you all over again."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3f5f47cb-888f-4263-a168-357fa15f40a2",
                                "sense_id": "e6230e03-009f-3067-b8c0-ad8c84d3ff22",
                                "text": "\"And this little lovely standing next to him is my favorite heartbreaker, The Fair Lady Sara from Samaria. Kids, this is Dr. Donovan.\" Sara beamed, obviously thrilled at being considered anyone's heartbreaker, especially Uncle Erik's."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "16612f4d-d487-4e65-a999-c417b1a34f27",
                                "sense_id": "e6230e03-009f-3067-b8c0-ad8c84d3ff22",
                                "text": "I imagined him as the kind of boy who knows girls are equals; the teen with female friends as well as male; then a kind man, a good man, the kind of man who knows better than to be a heartbreaker, despite his looks."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ac618a68-8021-3349-9da2-29013173c0a1",
                        "entry_id": "48d9439f-d217-3cc8-8933-2e64d68b474c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Someone or something that breaks someone's heart, as:",
                            "Something that causes sorrow, grief or extreme disappointment."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "agent"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "93b3deb4-2e28-47e8-bb6d-0b7a6ec6a845",
                                "sense_id": "ac618a68-8021-3349-9da2-29013173c0a1",
                                "text": "He's not lucid most of the time, and that's a heartbreaker. The LAPD will not release details on the altercation that earned Dudley Smith his wounds; they know he would prefer to spare the family of the robber he killed the ignominy of public ..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f579f991-0791-44e4-abd6-fe2b583e1ffe",
                                "sense_id": "ac618a68-8021-3349-9da2-29013173c0a1",
                                "text": "It's a heartbreaker, as I was reminded just now when I went to get the chapter reference, reread it, and started bawling."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1d98bdb5-3428-4d19-8f24-363d62f15c04",
                                "sense_id": "ac618a68-8021-3349-9da2-29013173c0a1",
                                "text": "It's a heartbreaker. The worst part of that situation was trying to console Grace. It was just awful. Don't let experiences like this make you bitter. The truth is, our kids are a challenge, and not everyone is going to want to join us in this journey."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "485bd5d3-2939-3801-9c51-58f000ab040c",
                        "entry_id": "48d9439f-d217-3cc8-8933-2e64d68b474c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Someone or something that breaks someone's heart, as:",
                            "A match which ends in defeat for a promising player or team."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "agent"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "65541ec2-bc72-4366-8ba6-a49da3d874ef",
                                "sense_id": "485bd5d3-2939-3801-9c51-58f000ab040c",
                                "text": "Kansas appeared in its first bowl following the 1947 season, losing a heartbreaker to Georgia Tech in the Orange Bowl. KU landed in the Bluebonnet Bowl following the 1961 season, and beat up a good Rice squad, 33-7."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "15ea849f-6513-4358-9eda-ba4444994291",
                                "sense_id": "485bd5d3-2939-3801-9c51-58f000ab040c",
                                "text": "Wyoming lost a heartbreaker 7–6. Utah's touchdown was scored on an intercepted pass, Wyoming missed an extra point and, most importantly, an official did not get downfield in time to see a punt hit a Utah player not once, but twice[…]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "33d548b6-1728-4c61-aff1-50c48bb54b15",
                                "sense_id": "485bd5d3-2939-3801-9c51-58f000ab040c",
                                "text": "In 1988 and again in 1989 the team went back to Bristol, Connecticut, for the nationals, coming in at third place one year and in second place another, losing the championship to Wisconsin-Oshkosh in a heartbreaker in eleven innings."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "84312b0d-a5df-3863-b611-d774369d9656",
                        "entry_id": "48d9439f-d217-3cc8-8933-2e64d68b474c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Someone or something that breaks someone's heart, as:",
                            "A curl or lovelock."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "agent",
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0df2c16b-37d0-4aa2-93e7-c63efa312c44",
                        "source_entry_id": "48d9439f-d217-3cc8-8933-2e64d68b474c",
                        "source_sense_description": "person who causes sorrow",
                        "target_lang_word": "casse-cœur",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
